   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "From symptom to cure",
     "texto": [
      "**Symptoms.** **Tengo mareos**, **náuseas**, **escalofríos**. **Me mareo** en el coche. **He perdido el apetito.**\n\n**At the surgery.** The doctor **te toma la tensión**, **te manda un análisis de sangre** or **una radiografía**, **te da un diagnóstico** and **te receta** a medicine. Sometimes you are sent to a specialist.\n\n**Illnesses.** An illness can be **leve**, **grave**, **crónica** or **contagiosa**. In formal language you **padecer** or **sufrir** an illness.\n\n**Passing it on.** **Me has contagiado la gripe.** **Me he contagiado.** **Vacunarse contra** la gripe.\n\n**Injuries.** **Hacerse un esguince**, **torcerse el tobillo**, **romperse** a bone. They **escayolan** your arm, put on **una venda**, give you **puntos** and you are left with **una cicatriz**.\n\n**The leaflet.** It gives **la dosis recomendada** and **los efectos secundarios**. A medicine may be **un calmante**, **un antiinflamatorio** or **una pomada**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Who acts and what would have happened",
     "texto": [
      "**When others act**, without saying who, Spanish uses the third person plural: **me hicieron una radiografía**, **le dieron cinco puntos**, **me pusieron una venda**.\n\n**Verbs with «se»**: **marearse**, **vacunarse**, **contagiarse**. **Vacunarse contra** la gripe.\n\n**De + compound infinitive** expresses a condition that was not met: **de no haberme caído, no me habría enterado** = if I had not fallen, I would not have found out."
     ],
